  "description": "Mount Roskill covers many of Auckland’s western suburbs, including Hillsborough, Lynfield, and Blockhouse Bay. The seat is held by National’s Carlos Cheung, who was first elected in 2023 with a margin of 15,659 votes. National also won the party vote with 43% of the vote, while Labour was second with 30%. Amusingly, the eponymous suburb of Mount Roskill is actually split between the Mount Albert and Mount Roskill electorates. \n\n",
